  "resolved_findings": [
    {
      "id": "P03-R01",
      "severity": "F1",
      "confidence": "high",
      "evidence_type": "static-proof",
      "finding": "The first wording could conflate 64-bit ISA address representation with the narrower actual device memory aperture.",
      "resolution": "Header, manifest and specification now name representation width explicitly, cite the inherited 48-bit RV64 memory width, and require trusted allocation/profile mapping validation before any future dispatch. Boundary encoding tests do not assert physical validity."
    },
    {
      "id": "P03-R02",
      "severity": "F1",
      "confidence": "high",
      "evidence_type": "missing-test",
      "finding": "Separate planner-field and encoder-byte tests could miss a planner that discarded successful encoded argument bytes.",
      "resolution": "The successful suballocation test now compares the entire returned 56-byte plan block with an independent literal containing nonzero offsets and actual checked addresses."
    }
  ],
  "static_findings_checked": [
    "Dimension and byte multiplication reject overflow before use; supported tuple checks prevent overflow in fixed encoder span calculations.",
    "Offset and span checks use subtraction after ordered bounds checks; base-plus-offset rejects addition overflow. Full allocation and selected range both fit the declared representation.",
    "Aliasing uses inclusive endpoints only after proven nonzero representable ranges, so endpoint additions cannot wrap. All three accesses are pairwise disjoint; adjacent slices are allowed.",
    "Repeated allocation IDs require consistent metadata. Device identity and access are checked independently of allocation-ID equality. Registry metadata and profile flags are explicitly trusted caller attestations, not authentication.",
    "Both output objects are initialized locally and published only after every validation/encoding stage succeeds. All failure paths preserve caller output.",
    "All eleven argument fields have explicit widths/offsets; 56-byte size and eight-byte alignment are statically asserted. Encoder emits each byte explicitly and does not serialize host pointers, native padding or size_t.",
    "Exact compact layouts, strides, six format/shape tuples, positive-zero initial accumulation, no transpose/batching and exact bounded profile agree across source, manifest and design.",
    "All successful plans retain execution_available=false. Unsupported families are explicitly unavailable. No runtime symbols, installed headers, install rule, production kernel or RTL/model source is changed.",
    "Ownership/async completion semantics are future-wrapper obligations; the pure planner neither owns nor releases resources and cannot certify actual queue, transfer or lifetime safety."
  ],
